         <photoshop:ColorMode>3</photoshop:ColorMode>
         <photoshop:ICCProfile>sRGB IEC61966-2.1</photoshop:ICCProfile>
         <photoshop:TextLayers>
            <rdf:Bag>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Managing your Sacred Space</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Managing your Sacred Space</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Meditation is not all about emptying the mind; the mind is alwa</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Meditation is not all about emptying the mind; the mind is always active, quite often narrating, guiding and directing our internal talk, most of which is contained within our belief systems. Meditation can calm and quiet the mind by becoming the observer of our thoughts, rather than sucked into the drama and ensuing emotions that lead to overwhelm, anxiety, worry, fear, anger, frustration.             As the world spins on its axis, we can experience our own rhythm and nature, receive inner wisdom and be guided soulfully by our inner community, our hearts and true self.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Before listening to these guided meditations, I invite you to s</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Before listening to these guided meditations, I invite you to spend 2-5 minutes in a meditative posture (sitting, or laying down) and see what sort of questions arise from this gentle experience. Allow your mind to be free and honour what comes.  After each meditation, sitting for some moments in reï¬‚ection is recommended. Having a pen and paper handy to record your thoughts, feelings and experiences invites the experience to be fully realised. It can also allow things to arise you didn't know were there! </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>A series of guided meditations to create  and cultivate your in</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>A series of guided meditations to create  and cultivate your inner sacred space</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Experience the Magic Within</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Experience the Magic Within</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Sacred Inner Space</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Sacred Inner Space</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Cultivating a</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Cultivating a</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>AmyGrist.com</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>AmyGrist.com</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
            </rdf:Bag>
         </photoshop:TextLayers>
